# Lessons Learned — Free Throw Frenzy

## Project Patterns
- CRA project bootstrapped with React 19; TypeScript added as a dependency.
- Game engine is pure TS with no React dependency for hot-loop performance.
- Canvas rendering and React HUD are separated; state flows via callbacks/refs.

## Preferences
- Minimal dependencies: no Phaser, Matter.js, or similar engines.
- Vector-only graphics (canvas arcs/rects) — no image assets for v1.
- Tailwind for all UI styling; no additional CSS frameworks.

## Known Challenges
- CRA + TypeScript requires renaming .js → .tsx and adding tsconfig.json.
- Mobile touch input needs `passive: false` for `touchstart` to prevent scroll.
- Canvas must resize responsively without losing aspect ratio.

## Decisions Log
